# SDK §5.2's shadow-stack default, restated so that a plain
# `cargo build --release --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` produces the same module
# `cargo eio build` does — the same property §5.1 asks of `[profile.release]`, kept for
# the one setting a `Cargo.toml` cannot carry.
#
# `wasm-ld` defaults the shadow stack to 1 MiB, which is a desktop linker's default and
# not a size anybody chose for a block: it makes a module declare 17 pages of linear
# memory, 1088 KiB, three and a half times the whole of a leaf's SRAM (LEAF §4.2). At
# {{stack_size}} bytes a block declares one page and nothing else about it changes.
#
# Raise it here if this block genuinely needs a deeper stack. `[target.<triple>]`
# outranks the `build.rustflags` `cargo eio build` passes, so editing this array is the
# one edit that moves both build paths together. A block that declares more than one
# page is still a valid block — a leaf firmware build is where it is refused, and that
# is the only place that knows the per-instance page budget to refuse it against.
[target.wasm32-unknown-unknown]
rustflags = ["-C", "link-arg=-zstack-size={{stack_size}}"]
